### Lab 3 - Books REST API requests
### Start your server before running these requests.
### VS Code extension: REST Client
### Local base URL
@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000

### 1. Get all books
GET http://localhost:3000/books/

### 2. Get one book (change the ID if needed)
GET http://localhost:3000/books/3/

### 3. Search books by title
GET http://localhost:3000/books/?search_q=Atomic

### 4. Sort books by price in ascending order
GET http://localhost:3000/books/?order_by=price&order=ASC

### 5. Sort books by title in descending order
GET http://localhost:3000/books/?order_by=title&order=DESC

### 6. Limit the number of books returned
GET http://localhost:3000/books/?limit=5

### 7. Pagination - skip the first 7 books and return the next 5
GET http://localhost:3000/books/?limit=5&offset=7

### 8. Filter books by minimum price
GET http://localhost:3000/books/?min_price=100

### 9. Filter books by maximum price
GET http://localhost:3000/books/?max_price=500

### 10. Filter books by a price range
GET http://localhost:3000/books/?min_price=100&max_price=500

### 11. Combine search, sorting, pagination, and price filters
GET http://localhost:3000/books/?search_q=The&order_by=title&order=ASC&min_price=100&max_price=500&limit=5&offset=0

### 12. Add a new book (successful POST; expected status: 201)
POST http://localhost:3000/books/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "The Pragmatic Programmer",
  "author": "Andrew Hunt",
  "price": 450,
  "pages": 320
}

### Check here for added books
GET http://localhost:3000/books/?limit=20




### 13. Add a book with missing title (validation test; expected status: 400)
POST http://localhost:3000/books/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "author": "Test Author",
  "price": 200,
  "pages": 150
}

### 14. Add a book with non-numeric price (validation test; expected status: 400)
POST http://localhost:3000/books/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Invalid Price Test",
  "author": "Test Author",
  "price": "two hundred",
  "pages": 150
}

### 15. Update a book (change the ID if needed; expected status: 200)
PUT http://localhost:3000/books/1/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Updated Book Title",
  "author": "Updated Author",
  "price": 350,
  "pages": 250
}

### 16. Request a book ID that does not exist (expected status: 404)
GET http://localhost:3000/books/999999/

### 17. Delete a book (change the ID to a test book; expected status: 200)
DELETE http://localhost:3000/books/11/

### 18. Delete a book ID that does not exist (expected status: 404)
DELETE http://localhost:3000/books/999999/
